+        # 6. Render
+        C = rasterize(mesh, color)
+        
+        return C
 ```
 
+**Parameters:**
+*   **D (Cascaded Levels):** Default 3 [S1].
+*   **MLP_c Architecture:** Two-layer MLP, 128 nodes per layer, ReLU activation [S1].
+*   **Optimizer:** Adam [S1].
+*   **Learning Rates:** CasCPRF: 0.02; MLP_c: 0.0001 [S1].
+*   **Training Config (Exploration):** 30,000 iterations, batch size 4096, single Nvidia A100 GPU (40GB), ~25 minutes [S1].
+*   **Delta_m Initialization:** Random within $[-0.3, 0.3]$ [S1].
+*   **Albedo ($b_d$) Constraint:** Min/Max within $[0, 1]$ [S1].
+*   **Roughness ($r$) Constraint:** Minimum value 0.08 [S1].
+*   **Environment Lighting Initialization:** Randomly initialized as 0.5 [S1].
+*   **Exploitation Optimizer:** Adam, Learning Rate 0.03 (falloff from 1.0 to 0.1 exponentially), 5,000 iterations, batch size 8 images (512x512), single NVIDIA A100 GPU (40GB), ~1 hour [S1].
+
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Spectral Bias:** The method addresses the difficulty MLPs have in learning high-frequency contents due to rapid eigenvalue spectrum decay in the Neural Tangent Kernel (NTK) [S1].
+*   **Topology Noise:** The preliminary mesh extracted via Marching Cubes may contain high-frequency noise, which is addressed by the topology finetune stage [S1].
+*   **Convergence Speed:** Volumetric texture learning can converge slowly and produce overly-smoothed results; CasCPRF avoids this by using fixed 2D texture indices from an input mesh [S1].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Exploration stage takes ~25 minutes on a single Nvidia A100 GPU (40GB) for 30,000 iterations with batch size 4096 [S1]. Exploitation stage takes ~1 hour on a single Nvidia A100 GPU (40GB) for 5,000 iterations with batch size 8 (512x512) [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the voxel grid size ($125^3$ to $250^3$) and the number of cascaded levels ($D=3$). The tensor decomposition provides a compact representation compared to dense voxel grids [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Produces superior reconstruction quality compared to single-scale counterparts with the same model size budget. The separation of frequency bands allows efficient learning of both specular patterns (low spatial/high angular frequency) and texture details (high spatial/low angular frequency) [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires an initial mesh for texture indexing in the exploitation stage. The two-stage process (exploration then exploitation) increases total training time compared to single-stage NeRF variants.
-*   **When to use:** When high-fidelity novel view synthesis and physically-based material/lighting estimation are required, and computational resources (GPU memory and time) allow for a two-stage optimization process.
